<script>
  import reports from '#lib/data/reports-4471.json';
  import notes from '#lib/data/desk-notes.json';
  import { groupByCause, readAs, uniqueById } from '#lib/kb/causes';
  import { tenantOf } from '#lib/kb/locales';
  import CauseTable from '#lib/kb/CauseTable.svelte';
  import RenderStamp from '#lib/kb/RenderStamp.svelte';

  // Counted the way CauseTable counts #4471.
  const groups = groupByCause(uniqueById(reports).filter((r) => r.mergedInto === 4471), tenantOf);
  const hint = groups.find((g) => g.cause === 'hint').reports.length;
  const oneDayMove = groups.reduce((n, g) => n + readAs(g, notes.oneDayMove), 0);
</script>

[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) holds every report about a wrong date and calls them one issue with
one fix queued. Most of its reports share one cause, the parser, and #4471 is that ticket. Two
other problems sit inside it, and the queued fix covers neither. Each now has its own ticket:

